{"`canManage()` checks for `VIEW` and `MANAGE` scopes, making it equivalent to `canView()`. It should only check for `MANAGE`, consistent with `canManage(GroupModel group)`. As written, a user with only the `VIEW` scope will pass the manage check.": 0.9830046892166138, "`groupResource.getId()` returns the authorization resource's internal ID, not the group ID. The `hasPermission` method looks up resources by name (`findByName`), and callers of `getGroupIdsWithViewPermission` expect actual group IDs. Use `groupResource.getName()` instead, which holds the group ID used as the resource name.": 0.9568727016448975, "The feature-flag guard only checks V1 (`ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ`), but V2 (`ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2`) can be enabled independently. When only V2 is active, this listener is never registered, so removing a role, client, or group won't clean up its associated permissions \u2014 they become orphaned. The condition should mirror the pattern in `MgmtPermissions` constructor and check for either feature.": 0.9195433855056763, "Removing the `!auth.users().canView()` guard means that admins with full user-view permission will now have their user search narrowed to group members whenever `getGroupIdsWithViewPermission()` returns a non-empty set. Previously, full-view users bypassed group filtering entirely. This can cause admins to silently see fewer users than they're authorized to view.": 0.11785883456468582, "This filter drops globally authorized users in V2: `canView(GroupModel)` does not include `canView()` global permission, so subgroup results can be incorrectly empty.": 0.15049715340137482, "`@return` says \"Stream of IDs\" but the method returns `Set<String>`. Likely leftover from a previous signature.": 0.11781560629606247, "Javadoc references `canManageMembership` but this is `requireManageMembers` \u2014 it should reference `canManageMembers(GroupModel)`. Looks like a copy-paste from the `requireManageMembership` Javadoc above.": 0.23408034443855286, "Newly created `testGroup` is not added to test cleanup, which can leak state across tests and cause order-dependent failures.": 0.06343430280685425, "`resolveGroup` lacks a fallback lookup by name, unlike `resolveUser` (which falls back to `getUserByUsername`) and `resolveClient` (which falls back to `getClientByClientId`). If a caller passes a group name instead of a UUID, the resolution will fail.": 0.46899843215942383, "This drops the global view-permission bypass. In V2 permissions, `canView()` can be granted via the all-groups resource even when `canView(group)` is false for specific group resources, so the new filter can hide groups a user is allowed to see. Preserve the global permission short-circuit.": 0.169971764087677, "Typo: \"it's clientId\" should be \"its clientId\" (possessive, not contraction).": 0.053408749401569366, "Double semicolon `;;` \u2014 remove the extra semicolon.": 0.09187687188386917}